# Performance (all changes)

Full detail: `docs/performance.md`.

## Database

- Integer PKs; index columns in hot-path `WHERE` / `JOIN` / `ORDER BY` (see `docs/db-schema.md` indexes)
- Default queries exclude soft-deleted rows (`deletedAt IS NULL`)
- Avoid N+1: use JOIN / TypeORM `relations`, not per-row queries in loops
- List endpoints: `select` only needed columns; paginate (default 50, max 200)

## Dashboard & aggregation

- Live `COUNT` / `GROUP BY` — no summary table unless Decision #10 is updated
- Exclude `renewed` and `archived` from metrics

## Expiry job

- Snapshot-first: paginate all GETs, then PATCH in batches (max 200)
- Skip unchanged records (computed status matches current `status`)
- Exponential backoff + timeout on HTTP and EventBridge calls

## API & frontend

- Paginated responses; never unbounded list returns
- Deep offset pagination is acceptable at current scale; prefer indexes over full scans

When planning features, note query patterns, expected row counts, and index needs before coding.
